.TH "STYLEPROPERTYMAP.APPEND" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
StylePropertyMap.append \- StylePropertyMap: append() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]append()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]StylePropertyMap\f[R] interface adds one or more values to the end
of a list\-valued CSS property\(cqs value list.
.PP
A list\-valued CSS property is one whose value is a comma\-separated
list of terms, such as \f[CR]background\-image\f[R] or
\f[CR]animation\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
append(property)
append(property, value1)
append(property, value1, value2)
append(property, value1, value2, /* \&..., */ valueN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]property\f[R]
An identifier indicating the stylistic feature (e.g., font, width,
background color) to add.
.TP
\f[B]value1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]valueN\f[R]
One or more values to add to the end of \f[CR]property\f[R]\(cqs value
list, in the order given.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]property\f[R] is not a valid CSS list\-valued property.
.IP \(bu 2
Any of \f[CR]value1\f[R], \&..., \f[CR]valueN\f[R] is already associated
with a different property (for example, a value read from one
property\(cqs entry in a \f[CR]StylePropertyMap\f[R], then passed to
\f[CR]append()\f[R] for another property).
.IP \(bu 2
Any of \f[CR]value1\f[R], \&..., \f[CR]valueN\f[R] is a
\f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] or \f[CR]CSSVariableReferenceValue\f[R]
object.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]property\f[R]\(cqs current value contains a \f[CR]var\f[R]
reference.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example shows an extra background image value being added to the
\f[CR]background\-image\f[R] property of the element, using
\f[CR]HTMLElement.attributeStyleMap\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// get the button element\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] buttonEl = document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq);

\f[I]// append another value to the background\-image property set on the attribute\f[R]
buttonEl.attributeStyleMap.append(
  \(dqbackground\-image\(dq,
  \(dqlinear\-gradient(180deg, blue, black)\(dq,
);
.EE
